{
  "schema": "rhlean-semantic-facets/1",
  "status": "SEARCH HEURISTIC, NOT A MATHEMATICAL CLAIM",
  "disclaimer": [
    "Every tag in this file is a lexical or syntactic hint used to rank where a",
    "human or agent should look next. A shared `carrier` tag does NOT mean two",
    "declarations are about the same object, and matching facets are NOT evidence",
    "that a bridge theorem is true or even plausible.",
    "AGENTS.md is explicit: never infer that two quantities are equal because their",
    "prose descriptions sound similar; use or prove an exact bridge theorem.",
    "This layer exists only to shorten the candidate list that then gets checked",
    "against compiled Lean source."
  ],
  "matching": [
    "A declaration matches a facet value if its name tokens (camelCase and",
    "snake_case split, lowercased) contain every token of any one `tokens` group,",
    "or if its module path contains one of `modules`. Statement-shape roles are",
    "matched against the declaration's statement text instead, which is structural",
    "rather than lexical and therefore the most reliable signal here."
  ],
